Tables

A table has 2 parts  --> Data + Metadata

Data -- stored in files ( in your own cloud account)
Metadata -- stored in Metastore  -- Eg:- Hive Metastore ( a legacy one in Databricks)

Each workspace will have its own hive meta-store ( a legacy feature)
A hive meta-store has 2 level namespace 
Schema/database + table name

issues with Hive meta-store
 - Hive meta-store offers basic metadata management but lacks fine grained access controls
 - it lacks built in data governance features like 
	- data lineage
	- auditing
	- access controls
	These limitations makes it challenging to manage security and compliance

   More over hive meta-store can deal only with structured data

Tables in hive meta-store do not benefit from the full set of security and governance features provided by the unity catalogue such as built n auditing , lineage and access control

Now in the latest version of data bricks workspace the unity catalogue enabled
Now whenever we create a databricks workspace, we will get an automatically provisioned unity catalogue meta-store..

A catalogue is named after your workspace

At the very top we have


Metastore
|
Catalog
|
Schema/Databases
|
Tables

so inside  meta-store -->catalogue --> Schema --> Tables

Meta-store will store metadata and security related config

Only one meta-store for each region

if we create a workspace in central India, then a new meta-store will be created in this region
if we create new workspace in this region, the workspace will be attached to this meta-store.
For every workspace there will be a new catalogue with the name similar to workspace, also in this default catalogue we will have 2 Schema (default & information_schema)


Can one workspace have more than one meta-store?
No it can't have

Can one meta-store be associated with multiple workspace?
It can be if the workspace are in the same region

The best practise is to have 1 meta-store in 1 region and then attach all workspace to the meta-store in that region


Two workspaces cannot share the same managed resource group name in Databricks


In Databricks hive meta-store is replaced by Unity catalogue
Unity catalogue is used to handle Metadata and for Governance
To use Unity catalogue meta-store is necessary

Unity catalogue meta-store has 3 level name space 


