To set the location for a table in databricks:

A table data can be stored at meta-store level or catalogue  level  or schema level

Whenever we create a workspace , a storage account location is not associated with it.

We can set the storage location at meta-store level, but it is recommended to store the data at catalog level, this can be done using azure databricks account portal
Meta-store level storage is not recommended as it will restrict to maintain the strict separation of storage across catalogs or environments(workspaces).

If we set the storage level at meta-store, by default managed table data will store in it.

By default managed table data is stored at catalog level,

