External tables

Tables with specifed external loc while creation are External tables

Unity catalog  governs 
data access permissions but does not manage data life cycle , optmiations , storage location or layout
Unity catalog priviliges are not enforeced when user access data friles fro  external systems

Dropping an external table, will not have effect on data files.

When you create an external table, 
we can either register an existing directory of data file as table
or 
provide a path to create a new dir


Databricks recommends using external tables for the following use cases:
	- Need to resister a table backed by existing data that is not compatible with unity catalog managed tables 
	- required a direct access to the data from non databricks clients


